@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@customerId = 1

### Create (201). Repeating this returns 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Kamau",
  "email": "john.kamau@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0712345678"
}

### List (page defaults to 1, pageSize to 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers?page=1&pageSize=10

### Get (set customerId to the ID returned by POST)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### Update (keeping this customer's email is valid)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Kamau",
  "email": "john.kamau@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+254722334455"
}

### Invalid input (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": " ",
  "lastName": "Kamau",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "phoneNumber": ""
}

### Unknown customer (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/2147483647

### API information
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### OpenAPI document (development only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json
